<http://data.silknow.org/object/d8b3209f-97c0-3c3e-93a0-7e26e7ebad1a/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Border of brocaded silk. With a blue textured ground on which is a large-scale floral design mainly in pink, green and golden-yellow. From top to bottom, the flowers used are chrysanthemums, sunflowers, roses and tulips. There are narrow borders on each side containing formal decoration.\n\nThe silk has a cannellé ground and the pattern is brocaded, bound in tabby by a binding warp of cream silk, one binding warp thread and eight ground warp threads. There is a selvedge on the left hand side 1.2 cms wide, with 6 outer cordonnets, 8 warp threads each consisting of 3 to 4 threads, and the rest of the selvedge is woven in blue tabby."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d8b3209f-97c0-3c3e-93a0-7e26e7ebad1a> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/d8b3209f-97c0-3c3e-93a0-7e26e7ebad1a/domain/2>
