        rdfs:comment                   "Border of brocaded silk, France, 1775-1800"@en , "Border of brocaded silk. With a blue textured ground on which is a large-scale floral design mainly in pink, green and golden-yellow. From top to bottom, the flowers used are chrysanthemums, sunflowers, roses and tulips. There are narrow borders on each side containing formal decoration.\n\nThe silk has a cannellé ground and the pattern is brocaded, bound in tabby by a binding warp of cream silk, one binding warp thread and eight ground warp threads. There is a selvedge on the left hand side 1.2 cms wide, with 6 outer cordonnets, 8 warp threads each consisting of 3 to 4 threads, and the rest of the selvedge is woven in blue tabby."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/5782fea4-7e94-3596-a54c-c34612cfef2c> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Border of brocaded silk. With a blue textured ground on which is a large-scale floral design mainly in pink, green and golden-yellow. From top to bottom, the flowers used are chrysanthemums, sunflowers, roses and tulips. There are narrow borders on each side containing formal decoration.\n\nThe silk has a cannellé ground and the pattern is brocaded, bound in tabby by a binding warp of cream silk, one binding warp thread and eight ground warp threads. There is a selvedge on the left hand side 1.2 cms wide, with 6 outer cordonnets, 8 warp threads each consisting of 3 to 4 threads, and the rest of the selvedge is woven in blue tabby."@en , "Border of brocaded silk, France, 1775-1800"@en ;
